AB  - This chapter presents the development of an intelligent supply chain control tower (iSCCT). Despite the developments in artificial intelligence (AI), including generalized AI, like Large Language Models (LLMs), few companies know how to use them to transform their traditional supply chains (SCs). This chapter presents key capabilities of iSCCT, i.e., Intelligent Visibility, Supply Chain Automation and Process Optimization, SC risk management, SC Planning and Execution. It demonstrates how a company (Zeta) transformed its supply chain into a 3-stage evolution: (1) Learning, where Zeta acquired knowledge from outsourcing the SCTT to its logistics partner. (2) Execution, where Zeta faced significant challenges, including software misalignments, poor internal integration, lack of top management support, and budget constraints. These challenges delayed the iSCCT implementation. Eventually, Zeta integrated Human, Operational, and Technological Intelligence into its iSCCT. (3) Growth phase, with increased automation and human-technology integration. The study shows how companies can internally develop an intelligent supply chain control tower. It discusses key takeaways for operations managers and researchers.
