AB  - Knowledge-guided reasoning offers a promising approach to enhancing multimodal intelligence in complex 3D environments. However, existing 3D vision–language models (VLMs) often exhibit limited spatial reasoning and generalization capabilities because of insufficient reasoning supervision and reliance on fixed viewpoint configurations. To address these limitations, we introduce KnowScene, a knowledge-guided framework that integrates structured chain-of-thought (CoT) supervision with reinforcement reasoning based on Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO). To provide structured supervision for model initialization, we construct a large-scale synthetic dataset, KnowScene-60K, using a rule-based data engine that generates and filters CoT samples from multiple 3D vision–language corpora. During reinforcement fine-tuning, KnowScene jointly optimizes perceptual grounding, semantic alignment, and format consistency through a multi-signal reward mechanism. An adaptive view selection module further strengthens cross-modal correspondence by dynamically prioritizing task-relevant viewpoints. Extensive experiments on ScanRefer, Nr3D, and ScanQA demonstrate that KnowScene achieves an average improvement of 7.3% over the strongest competing baselines across the primary evaluation metrics for 3D dense captioning, question answering, and visual grounding. These results demonstrate that KnowScene consistently improves reasoning coherence and spatial understanding across diverse 3D vision–language tasks.
ER  - 

