AB  - Generative artificial intelligence (AI) is playing an increasingly important role in transforming personalized drug development and improving safety within healthcare. This chapter introduces foundational generative models, including generative adversarial networks, variational autoencoders, and large language models. It discusses their utility in accelerating drug discovery by designing novel compounds with optimized therapeutic properties. Emphasis is placed on how generative AI integrates patient-specific genomic, transcriptomic, and clinical data to guide the creation of personalized therapeutics. Applications in predictive toxicology, adverse drug reaction mitigation, and modeling drug–drug interactions are critically analyzed with respect to improving patient safety. The chapter also examines the regulatory, ethical, and implementation challenges that arise when deploying AI-generated interventions in clinical settings. Ultimately, it highlights the potential of generative AI to enhance treatment efficacy, mitigate risk, and facilitate the development of precision therapeutics in modern healthcare systems.
