KW  - Question answering
KW  - Large language models reasoning
KW  - Dynamic knowledge graph reasoning
KW  - Retreival augmented generation
AB  - Large language models (LLMs) have demonstrated strong reasoning capabilities but often struggle with hallucination and outdated information when disconnected from trusted external knowledge. To address the hallucination problem, recent research has explored the integration of LLMs with knowledge graphs (KGs). KGs provide trusted, structured, and explainable factual knowledge, thereby offering reliable grounding for LLM outputs. However, most existing methods assume complete KGs, where all factual triples required to answer a query are present. In practice, even the widely used KGs such as Wikidata and DBpedia are incomplete or outdated. Hence, we propose Triple Play, a training-free framework for question answering over incomplete KGs (IKGQA). Triple Play combines LLM reasoning with retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) to identify missing or outdated triples and generate accurate replacements from external sources. The framework follows a structured process that integrates symbolic knowledge, real-time retrieval, and self-evaluating LLM prompts for dynamic KG refinement. We evaluated Triple Play on two datasets: WebQSP and CWQ, under varying KG incompleteness levels (20%–80%). Results on WebQSP showed that Triple Play consistently outperformed strong baselines, including generate-on-graph (GoG) and think-on-graph (ToG). For example, at 40% incompleteness, it achieved Hits@1 of 75.18%, compared with 66.6% (GoG) and 61.4% (ToG). Even under 80% incompleteness, it maintained robust performance (66.73%), while baselines degraded considerably. On CWQ, Triple Play maintained high performance across different incompleteness levels, achieving Hits@1 of 71.85% at 40% incompleteness, exceeding GoG (62.3%) and ToG (58.2%), and reaching 64.91% at 80% incompleteness, outperforming GoG (51.4%) and ToG (48.7%). These results demonstrated the effectiveness of integrating LLMs and RAG for real-time KG validation and evolution under missing knowledge. Implementation is available at GitHub Repository.
